PRSENSE(1)
PRSENSE — principled AI-assisted pull request review

⸻

NAME
prsense — CLI-first, self-hosted AI code reviewer

⸻

SYNOPSIS
prsense [command] [options] [target]

⸻

DESCRIPTION
PRsense is a command-line tool for reviewing code changes using large
language models with full repository context.

It is designed for senior developers who want intentional, inspectable,
and self-hosted reviews without relying on hosted SaaS platforms.

PRsense operates primarily on diffs and surrounding context, producing
structured review signals that prioritize clarity, correctness, and
maintainability.

PRsense may optionally run a background daemon for long-lived or
service-oriented workloads, but the CLI operates independently by
default.

⸻

COMMANDS

review      Review a code change and emit structured review signals
index       Index a repository for faster and deeper contextual reviews
doctor      Diagnose PRsense installation and runtime environment
daemon      Manage the PRsense background daemon
setup       Perform optional one-time setup checks
help        Show help for a command

⸻

COMMAND: daemon

NAME
prsense daemon — manage the PRsense background daemon

SYNOPSIS
prsense daemon  [options]

DESCRIPTION
Manages the lifecycle of the PRsense background daemon.

The daemon is an optional, long-lived process intended for
service-oriented use cases such as:
	•	continuous indexing
	•	CI or webhook-triggered reviews
	•	multi-request coordination
	•	future integrations (e.g. GitHub Apps)

The daemon is not required for normal CLI usage.
The CLI does not delegate review execution to the daemon by default.

SUBCOMMANDS

prsense daemon start
Start the PRsense daemon in the background.

SYNOPSIS
prsense daemon start [–foreground]

OPTIONS
–foreground
Run the daemon in the foreground and log to stdout.

By default, the daemon runs in the background and listens on a local
socket or port.

prsense daemon stop
Stop a running PRsense daemon.

SYNOPSIS
prsense daemon stop

This sends a termination signal and waits for in-flight jobs to finish
before shutting down.

prsense daemon status
Show the current daemon status.

SYNOPSIS
prsense daemon status

Reports whether the daemon is running and, if so, its process ID.

NOTES
	•	The daemon is started and stopped explicitly.
	•	PRsense does not auto-start background processes.
	•	Daemon lifecycle is managed by OS signals, not HTTP APIs.

⸻

COMMAND: setup

NAME
prsense setup — perform optional one-time setup checks

SYNOPSIS
prsense setup

DESCRIPTION
Performs non-destructive setup validation and guidance.

This command is intended to help first-time users ensure that required
dependencies and configuration are in place.

Unlike prsense doctor, this command focuses on initial readiness rather
than ongoing diagnostics.

CHECKS PERFORMED
	•	Configuration file discovery
	•	Environment variable presence
	•	LLM provider availability
	•	Optional database or vector store connectivity
	•	File system permissions

No background services are started automatically.

EXAMPLES
prsense setup

⸻

COMMAND: review

NAME
prsense review — review a code change

SYNOPSIS
prsense review [target] [options]

DESCRIPTION
Reviews a code change and produces structured review signals.

The review analyzes:
	•	the diff itself
	•	surrounding code context
	•	repository conventions
	•	test and documentation impact

The default output is human-readable text suitable for terminal usage.
Machine-readable JSON output is also supported.

TARGETS
The review target may be one of:

.                       Current repository (default)
                  Path to a local repository
             Git revision range (e.g. origin/main..HEAD)
            Unified diff file
	•	

                  Read diff from stdin



OPTIONS
–base-branch
Override the base branch used for diff comparison.

–max-signals 
Maximum number of review signals to emit.

–confidence <0-1>
Minimum confidence required for a signal to be reported.

–context 
Maximum number of context chunks retrieved during review.

–no-context
Perform a diff-only review without contextual retrieval.

–explain
Include reasoning details and context references in output.

–format <text|json>
Output format. Default is text.

EXAMPLES
prsense review .
prsense review origin/main..HEAD
prsense review diff.patch
git diff | prsense review -
prsense review . –confidence 0.7 –max-signals 5

